Title: NIGHT SHIFT
Credit: Written by
Author: Jo Writer

INT. MARA'S APARTMENT - NIGHT

Rain streaks the window. *MARA* (30s) stares at an **unplugged** phone, and the _well-known_ silence presses in.
She does not move.

MARA
(to herself)
He is not going to call. He is not going to call, and that is fine.

JONAH (V.O.)
Mara, it's me.

MARA ^
Don't.

BRICK
Screw retirement.

STEEL ^
(grinning)
Screw retirement, too.

> THE END <

CUT TO:

EXT. ROOFTOP - CONTINUOUS

Wind. A water tower groans.

> FADE OUT.
